  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Bikes X" id="55d7-55ab-3d52-5a86" hidden="false">
      <description>When outside a Zone, this Infantry Unit is treated as a Vehicle with an A value of X, although Blast Weapons still inflict D6 hits against them. In addition, Bikes have Resilient and are not affected by Devastator, and are still treated as Infantry for RM tokens placed by enemy Decon weapons (see Bioficer Weapon Special Rules). Small Arms Weapons always treat units with Bikes as Infantry, meaning they cannot combine attacks and inflict 1 DP per hit. Bikes units outside Zones may always roll their DF against Small Arms hits, even if not Obscured. They may still enter Zones. Bikes lose any Ev and Weapons while Occupying.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Firing Ports" id="9fd5-35bf-980d-afb2" hidden="false">
      <description>If an Infantry Unit will not Embark/Disembark from this Transport in its activation, this Transport gains that Infantry Unit&apos;s Weapons that activation, except those with a R of CC. Those Weapons&apos; MA become Full and they lose Assault. This is cumulative with multiple Infantry Units. Those Weapons suffer -1Ac if this Transport Disembarks or moves over 0&quot; that activation.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flexible Capacity" id="ca18-9713-f6a9-42ac" hidden="false">
      <description>This Transport may be taken if at least half full.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ram" id="24b3-41ae-6020-a667" hidden="false">
      <description>You may only attack with this Weapon after moving and if its Unit may use its full move. If you attack with it, its Unit counts as moving its full Mv. Directly after the attack, this Weapon&apos;s Unit loses 1DP on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Subterranean" id="f25e-e18f-c83c-24b3" hidden="false">
      <description>If your Army contains Subterranean Units, any of your Groups may start the game in Holding. The entire Group, including its transports, must be able to disembark from the Subterranean Units in your army, or be embarked in Transports capable of doing so. Unarmed Subterranean Units do not count against your number of allowed Groups. Subterranean Units with a Transport Symbol are not taken with any Units aboard. When a Subterranean Squad enters from Ready, it may be placed on Good or Exceptional Ground anywhere on the Table. If it is unarmed, it cannot activate from then on. Squads in Holding may Disembark from ANY Subterranean Unit(s) providing their Transport Symbols match. Squads which Embark into Subterranean Units are placed into Holding. Any Objects carried by Units Embarking into it leave the Table. Any Units which Embark cannot re-enter the Table that Round or next Round. Squads may Embark or Disembark into or from a Subterranean Unit outside of that Subterranean Unit&apos;s activation. All other Embarking/Disembarking rules and restrictions still apply. Additionally, Subterranean Units may not Embark/Disembark more than their Symbol indicates per Round, but they may do both. For example, one with 6 could Embark 6, then Disembark 6. Units in Holding at the end of the game only count as destroyed if you have no Units which could return them to the Table if there were another Round.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Subterranean Small" id="02a2-5f02-2805-10df" hidden="false">
      <description>Only Vehicles with an initial DP of 1, and Infantry, can Embark or Disembark into or from this Unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Subterranean Medium" id="6ef7-734a-d64c-fbf1" hidden="false">
      <description>Only Vehicles with an initial DP of 1-2, and Infantry, can Embark or Disembark into or from this Unit.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
